    "description": "One line across a band: a note and the link that answers it. Hovering the link springs an icon up over it that never settles, a key melting into a lock and on into a bolt. The swap is not a crossfade: each glyph blurs as it leaves and unblurs as it arrives, and a steep alpha ramp over the pair thresholds the softened shapes back into solid mass, so one collapses into a droplet and the droplet hardens into the next. Nothing fades, since a fade under that ramp would only blink out. The whole cycle is one keyframe run three times a third apart, so exactly one glyph is at rest at any moment, and the paint is a gradient read off the palette rather than three frozen values. Reduced motion drops the filter and holds the first glyph still.",
