    "description": "A contact card: the team on one side, the ask on the other. The photos are prints dropped on a table, and the top one is on a spring. It does not sit under the pointer but eases toward it on a frame rate independent loop, and past a slack radius it spends only a fraction of the extra distance, so a long pull feels like dragging something heavy. Let go anywhere and it snaps back to the bottom of the stack, leaving the next print facing up: there is no throw distance to clear, so a longer drag only buys a longer look underneath. The offset is zeroed in the same commit that turns the deck, so the print arriving at the front starts centred rather than flying in from where the last one was let go. Every print writes the standalone translate, rotate and scale properties, so the drag and the deck's fan never compose into one string, and each step back in the fan is a fraction of the one before rather than another whole step, so a deck of eight is barely wider than a deck of three. The sources are props, so the card carries as many prints as you point it at.",
