    "description": "The stitch button with the dash set walking. Two plates, one inside the other: the outer is the button's real box and carries only a fill, the inner is the same shape inset by 2px on every side with a dashed rim stroked on its own edge, so the chip keeps the size scale's outside dimensions and the label sits exactly where the matte button's label sits. On hover the dash marches clockwise, and that is one animated property, stroke-dashoffset counting down by exactly one dash period, so the loop is seamless and the rect's own direction supplies the clockwise part. Nothing moves in the layout and nothing repaints but the stroke. The keyframe runs paused rather than starting at hover, because starting it would snap the dash back to phase zero every time the pointer arrives; paused, it holds wherever it stopped and picks up from there. A speed prop sets how long one period takes, reduced motion stops the march outright, and sizes and the leading icon come from the matte button, so it sits on the same scale and takes path data, an image src or a lucide glyph alike.",
