    "title": "Sweep Card ID",
    "summary": "The Sweep Card cut to an ID badge: the same holographic band crossing the card under the pointer, on a container the width of a shadcn card rather than a box that grows with its copy, so the card keeps its shape whatever the title says.",
    "description": "The Sweep Card cut to an ID badge: the same holographic band crossing the card under the pointer, on a container the width of a shadcn card rather than a box that grows with its copy, so the card keeps its shape whatever the title says. The 0.718 ratio is the Contact CTA's ID card ratio, applied to that width, so the height follows the card rather than the viewport and the badge sizes like every other card in the kit. The band is a fixed gradient behind a moving mask rather than a background pan, so mask-position animates on the compositor and the card never repaints, and it is gated on real hover so a tap on a phone cannot park the band mid-card. The photo fills the badge and the copy sits under it, since a badge is read from the bottom up and a title floating in the middle of a portrait frame reads as a poster instead. The photo is a prop, and the well keeps its frame when there is none, so an install without artwork is still badge-shaped rather than collapsed. The edge is the same 4px rim, and the card's overflow is what cuts the band to the corners. Title and subtitle are props, the sweep is pure CSS, and the block ships with no dependencies and no client boundary. Dropped under prefers-reduced-motion.",
