    "description": "The knob toggle with the light show taken out: same moulded housing, same glyph that reshapes rather than crossfading, but nothing sweeps the rim when the theme flips, so the only thing that moves is the mark itself. Three circles' worth of edge come out of two pseudo elements and no extra nodes, since dropping the sweep drops the span it rode on; the collar is a plain disc sitting two pixels proud of the face and behind it, so all that shows of it is a ring, and the hairline inside the face is an inset shadow rather than a border, because a border would move the box. Only the knob answers the pointer: the button drops out of hit testing and the face opts back in, which is why hovering the housing does nothing while hovering the face dims the mark. The mark is painted by a gradient rather than currentColor and every id is namespaced with useId, so two of these on a page do not share a mask. Every colour is a theme token, with no second hue to re-tint for a palette. Ships controlled as ThemePlainKnob for a project already running next themes, with a default export that wires the dark class for one that is not.",
