    "name": "screen-wash-01",
    "title": "Screen Wash",
    "summary": "A screen: an aqua to navy wash under six faint columns, framed by an 8px rim.",
    "description": "A screen: an aqua to navy wash under six faint columns, framed by an 8px rim. The glass is inset by the bezel and rounded inside it, at the body's radius less the bezel's width, so the two corners are concentric the way a real display's are; run full bleed instead, the artwork keeps square corners behind a rounded case. The rim is an inset ring on a layer over the artwork rather than one on the plate, since an inset ring paints above an element's own background but below its children and would sit under the full bleed wash. Hover lifts the wash from resting to lit and nothing else moves, because the wash is its own layer under the columns: one opacity animates and the gradient never repaints. The panel keeps its own two palettes rather than taking the page's, since it reads as a device and a lit display stays lit whichever theme the page is in. One component and one stylesheet, no dependencies and no client hooks, and the lift is gated on a real pointer so a tap cannot leave the screen stuck lit.",
